WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.967
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.235
CHARLES M. BLOW:
<i> I'm trying to find a way</i>

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.339
<i> we can lift the burden
 off the shoulders</i>

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.508
<i> of Black people,
 of white supremacy.</i>

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.011
What if we skip over
all that hoping?

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.814
What if we skip over
all the pleading and the begging

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.717
and the marching
and the shouting

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:18.952
and go straight
to the power?

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.455
<i> During the Great Migration,
 about six million Black people</i>

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.224
left the South for cities
in the North and West.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.460
<i> I suggest that Black people
 return to the states</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.296
<i> with the highest percentages
 already of Black people,</i>

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.365
<i> where they can gain
 political power.</i>

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.301
If we're gonna make a go of it,
the South makes a lot of sense.

00:00:38.103 --> 00:00:39.706
CHARLES:<i> I was shaking
 and nervous,</i>

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:43.843
<i> maybe even afraid about
 leaving New York for Atlanta.</i>

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.211
I have convinced myself
that this is

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.847
<i> what we must do
 as Black people.</i>

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:51.217
SPEAKER:<i> I don't know if you
could convince that many people</i>

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.418
<i> to move that way.</i>

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.721
The argument of like,
"I ain't going South,"

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:55.922
is that much different from,

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.590
"Hey, up North,
let's get this together."

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.560
You are encouraging
Black Chicago to stay here,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.429
-stay intact.
-I am. This is our city.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:08.034
I want for Black boys to live
in a world

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.336
<i> where they do not have
 to think about</i>

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.305
<i> protecting their humanity.</i>

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.508
Those who don't want to see
sharing of that power

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.010
<i> will do all that they can
 to waylay that situation.</i>

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.445
SPEAKER 2:
<i> There is the X factor</i>

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:21.347
<i> of these
 voter suppression bills.</i>

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:24.150
Every freedom is at stake.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:28.488
There are some things in life
that are bigger than you.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.891
<i> It has to be about
 community success.</i>

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.759
We are the cavalry
we've been waiting on.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.328
I have to figure out
if I am

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:41.468
<i>being an apostle of Black power
 or am I chasing windmills.</i>

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:46.038
We gotta get back and claim,
really, what we built.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.708
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

